
"smart_sources:Lore for Flora's Regency Era (UPDATED)/culture/Culture - The Faith of Althena.md": {"path":"Lore for Flora's Regency Era (UPDATED)/culture/Culture - The Faith of Althena.md","last_embed":{"hash":null},"embeddings":{},"last_read":{"hash":"7uk7j8","at":1777331817895},"class_name":"SmartSource","last_import":{"mtime":1777016020648,"size":2052,"at":1777331817922,"hash":"7uk7j8"},"blocks":{"#---frontmatter---":[1,23],"#Culture - The Faith of Althena":[25,26],"#The central religion of Flora, shaping its laws and culture.":[27,38],"#The central religion of Flora, shaping its laws and culture.#{1}":[28,38]},"outlinks":[],"metadata":{"type":"lore","status":"active","priority":120,"tags":["#lorebook"],"keys":["althena","goddess","faith","religion","church","dogma"],"position":"after","depth":4,"scanDepth":1,"summary":"**What it is:** The central religion of Flora, based on worship of the Mother Goddess Althena. It establishes a female-led society where women lead due to inherent empathy, and men have a sacred duty to support and protect.\n\n**When selected:** Any scene involving Flora's laws, gender roles, family structures, religious ceremonies, or oracles (Seers). Also when characters discuss divine feminine worship, marriage/household duties, or the prophet Jonathan Harper.\n\n**Key relationships:** Althena (deity); Seers (male oracles); Jonathan Harper (original prophet); doctrine mentions a mysterious divine warrior consort."},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[]},"smart_blocks:Lore for Flora's Regency Era (UPDATED)/culture/Culture - The Faith of Althena.md#---frontmatter---": {"path":null,"last_embed":{"hash":null},"embeddings":{},"text":null,"length":0,"last_read":{"hash":"1gwykh4","at":1777331817895},"key":"Lore for Flora's Regency Era (UPDATED)/culture/Culture - The Faith of Althena.md#---frontmatter---","lines":[1,23],"size":816,"outlinks":[],"class_name":"SmartBlock"},
